<title>FRANCE: French farmers dump strawberries at Juppe office.</title>
<headline>French farmers dump strawberries at Juppe office.</headline>
<dateline>BORDEAUX, France 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>French strawberry farmers, protesting at a red menace of cheap imports, dumped 10 tonnes of their crop on Friday outside the city hall in Bordeaux, where Prime Minister Alain Juppe is mayor.</p>
<p>&quot;It's the first time we've been obliged to destroy strawberries,&quot; said Raymond Girardi, spokesman for the strawberry producers from the south-western Lot-et-Garonne area. &quot;We wanted the prime minister to benefit from it.&quot;</p>
<p>He said the growers, who also sold a truck-load of strawberries at rock-bottom prices on Thursday under the Eiffel Tower in Paris, wanted state subsidies to protect them from imports of low-priced strawberries from Spain and Morocco.</p>
</text>
